mantle rm295
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_dorcas_rainford
title the swimmer's floating hood
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=chatty humour=merry
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk floats_a_pebble_in_an_upturned_oilcloth_hood
likes roast_pork swimming fresh_straw misty_dawns
dislikes deep_mud early_bells
fears losing_sight_of_a_swimmer
hopes keeping_a_bright_mark_above_water
topics pastimes +0.6 weather +0.4 travel +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=frank refuse=plain tease=merry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# turns an oilcloth hood inside out to float a pebble and chatters cheerfully until a question deserves a straight answer.
words
oath! = Float my ears | Stiffen my hoodstring
saying! = Keep the bright patch showing | A splash wants a witness
hoodbowl = my upturned hood | a pocket of oilcloth
trim = a pale stitched rim | a bright strip of binding
tiebit = a long hood string | my good chin tie
carryrock = a flat grey stone | a water-smoothed pebble
oilmark = a dark oily trace | a speck of dressing
strawend = a twisted straw | a golden stalk
porkbit = a crisp curl of pork | a strip of roast rind
waterstep = a shallow ledge | a flat wading stone
knotbit = a loose running loop | an easy bow
springbit = a little spring in the weave | a yielding fold
mudcup = a deep heel print | a cup of dark mud

grown

opinion houses against 2 : I'd like the Houses to count every head home from their wharf work before counting the day's coin.
opinion strangers for 1 : Even a stranger's head is a head I'll keep in view when there's water about.
opinion festivals for 1 : A good chorus lets me join in without anyone hearing exactly which note I missed.
opinion watch mixed 1 : A uniform on a quay ought to be looking out towards the water as often as towards a purse.
opinion dole for 2 : Nobody needs to beat the tide on a belly filled only with pride.
opinion sump for 1 : I like a place where somebody'll laugh at a wet hood and still lend a dry bit of straw.
line greet : There's room beneath this ridiculous brim for a little talk.
line greet.return : I heard you. The hood hasn't folded over both ears yet.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I'll wake up when the talking gets interesting.
line farewell : Keep something bright where a friend can spot you.
line farewell.return : I'll wave the hood if I go past.
line again.open : Here comes the second splash of a good conversation.
line react.news : Set that floating where we can look properly.
line react.news.known : That's already been bobbing about my ears.
line react.news.new : Something new over the brim, for once.
line react.news.doubt : I'd test whether that floats before asking anyone to sail in it.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : That needs a good cheer with all the hoods thrown up.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I can stop making noise and stay close for that.
line answer.how : One ear folded flat but otherwise remarkably upright.
line ask.how : Keeping your chin clear of the day's splashes?
line decline : That sounds grand until somebody has to go in after the mess.
line thank : You kept the bright bit where I could find it.
line deflect_thanks : I'm fond of getting everybody home with the same number of toes.
line sympathise : I'll keep the noise down till your own words come clear.
line reassure : We can choose the shallow bit and start from there.
line ack : I can see that above the ripples now.
line offer : Pass me the dripping end. I'm already dressed for it.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My hood can swim with a pebble for a passenger. | Turn #hoodbowl# like this. Now it's a little boat.
b : How long before your passenger gets soaked?
a : Till I sneeze, usually. The captain's breath is the worst weather we get.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I watch for a greasy grip before lifting anything. | I've a flap of oilcloth between a slippery job and my sleeve.
b : Does it stay clean?
a : Certainly one side does. I've been searching for that side most of the week.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Learning goes better if I ask my question while the lesson's still warm. | I've been known to ask why the answer smells the way it does.
b : Ever get a straight answer?
a : Often. My trick is letting the person who's teaching me finish it.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My bright binding earns its keep when mist puts every coat in the same grey. | Morning mist delights me so long as my friends stay in sight.
b : Why keep a bright mark on you?
a : A voice can come from any part of the water. A mark puts a head at that exact spot.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The roast's best bit could just about mend a little hole in this hood. | I like crackling as stiff as the edge of a new brim.
b : Wouldn't that be rather greasy?
a : Gloriously. That's why the hole stays open and the pork goes in my mouth.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fresh straw belongs underfoot, except for one clean stalk I can chew. | I'm fond of the scratch of new bedding before it lies down and minds its manners.
b : Does that go with a wet coat?
a : Hang the coat up first, unless you want to wear it stuffed like a cushion.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can take a long swim cheerfully and still balk at six inches of mud. | Deep mud can have my footprint. It can't have the boot too.
b : How do you get free?
a : Wait till the ground's finished making that horrible sucking noise, then pull very slowly.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I think giving thanks for coming ashore ought to include counting who came with you. | A blessing can wait while you make sure all the swimmers have landed.
b : Even if you came in first?
a : Especially then. That's the swimmer with enough puff left to count.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can fit a day's worth of bad weather inside one rolled hood. | I never leave the hood behind just because the sky looks innocent.
b : What if it stays clear?
a : Then I've brought a cushion. A sensible garment can afford two occupations.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll laugh at a friend's wet backside after I know the rest of my friend is sound. | Getting somebody out of the water comes before naming the splash.
b : And after everybody's dry?
a : Then I'll give a perfectly fair account of how silly I looked getting in.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An early bell preys on the tender part of my ear beneath the brim. | You couldn't make a bell gentle by wrapping my head in another hood.
b : How would you wake folk instead?
a : Send a whiff of pork crackling up the stairs. I'd reach the bottom very briskly.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A damp tie pulled too tight will rub under the jaw. | After swimming I turn #tiebit# outside to air.
b : Would you leave it untied?
a : Only on land. A loose cord catching underwater would spoil an excellent afternoon.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm frank with anyone selling me a patch. It needs to float more than a sales pitch. | A cheap patch is expensive if I keep putting new ones over it.
b : How do you judge a patch?
a : Fold it twice, spring it open and look along the crease. A hole tells the truth promptly.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Poor weeks see my hood patched in three different colours. | When coin's narrow I make each scrap do its turn in the weather.
b : Mind wearing a bright patchwork?
a : It keeps me visible. I'm the only swimmer improving my outfit by running short of money.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A quiet moment at the wharf can hit me harder than a cold swim. | I don't laugh at folk counting who comes back up the quay.
b : Something happened there?
a : There's a loss I won't pretend away. I keep the sharp part out of a stranger's coat.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bird afloat gives me an unattainable example of looking composed. | I can keep my hood bobbing more neatly than my own head.
b : Is elegance important to a swimmer?
a : Only after breathing. I've been contentedly stuck on the first exercise for some time.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show a visitor the shallow approach first, even one who boasts a fine stroke. | A strong swimmer from elsewhere doesn't know our turns in the water.
b : Would you go in too?
a : If invited and if it's safe. Sometimes the better company is on shore with a good eye.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The words afloat are that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I heard a roundabout claim that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Would you swear to the story?
a : Only to having ears. The event never introduced itself to me.

story stone [topic=pastimes]
  : I set a pebble in my upturned hood and gave it a noble send-off.
  : The thing swung round in a circle till the pebble was looking straight back at me.
  b : Was the wind against it?
  : My chin string was still round my wrist. A short voyage with excellent arrangements for coming home.

story straw [topic=memories]
  : I stuffed the hood with straw to see how high it would ride.
  : It rode beautifully and strewed bright stalks halfway across a puddle.
  b : How did you recover your ship?
  : Followed the trail in very undignified little steps, collecting my bedding as I went.

story knot [topic=weather]
  : I pulled my hood tight against a mist and marched straight past my turning.
  : The air was quite clear by then, but I'd drawn the brim over both eyes.
  b : Any harm done?
  : Three paces. A wall acquainted itself with my nose and I reconsidered my arrangements.

rule @boat
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A passenger that size can sit right in the fold. | My hood takes a remarkably small fare.

rule @wake
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say If the bell's waiting for me it can have a long wait. | Good hour for looking at the light through one eye.

rule @work
when concept=bark self.apprentice=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I've a question somewhere under this hood. | Let me try that while the lesson's still in my fingers.

rule @dusk
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bright binding out before the day goes grey. | Last thing to vanish should be the swimmer's mark.
dlg resident.hub : Any subject you like, provided you're prepared for me to have an opinion.
dlg resident.job [self.job=laborer] : At #self.workplace# there's usually something that needs a steady pair of hands and an eye left open.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This washed up quite plainly. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : An account going round says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I wasn't there holding a lantern.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I can be perfectly serious while dressed like a floating tent.
dlg resident.bye : Come home with your ears in sight.

graft resident.hub
choice Will your hood take passengers? -> hood_passage
node hood_passage
say One pebble, sometimes two if both can be persuaded to sit in the middle. Nothing living till I've improved my seamanship.
choice What do you charge? -> hood_fee
choice I'll wave for it. -> hub
node hood_fee
say A cheerful wave from the bank. Nobody has yet persuaded a pebble to pay the fare.
choice I'll wave for it. -> hub
